[186,288,196],{},[186,290,291,292,295],{},"Static env vars (win over ",[145,293,294],{},"data","-derived vars)",[165,297,298,302,305,307],{},[186,299,300],{},[145,301,294],{},[186,303,304],{},"unknown",[186,306,196],{},[186,308,309,310,313,314,317],{},"Run parameters → ",[145,311,312],{},"SCREAMING_SNAKE"," env vars + ",[145,315,316],{},"SCHED_DATA"," (JSON)",[165,319,320,325,328,331],{},[186,321,322],{},[145,323,324],{},"timeoutMs",[186,326,327],{},"number",[186,329,330],{},"300000 (5 min)",[186,332,333,334,337,338,341,342,345],{},"Timeout: SIGTERM → 10s grace → SIGKILL → ",[145,335,336],{},"cancelled",". ",[145,339,340],{},"-1"," = ",[200,343,344],{},"no timeout"," — the container runs until it exits or is cancelled by the operator (matching the task-level run-deadline semantics)",[165,347,348,353,355,358],{},[186,349,350],{},[145,351,352],{},"maxLogKb",[186,354,327],{},[186,356,357],{},"10",[186,359,360],{},"Ring-buffer log cap",[165,362,363,368,372,374],{},[186,364,365],{},[145,366,367],{},"allowedTools",[186,369,193,370],{},[243,371],{},[186,373,196],{},[186,375,376,377,380,381],{},"Sandbox: images\u002Fcommands this task may run (",[145,378,379],{},"image@command"," specs) — see ",[382,383,385],"a",{"href":384},"..\u002Fsecurity","Security",[165,387,388,393,396,399],{},[186,389,390],{},[145,391,392],{},"envelope",[186,394,395],{},"boolean",[186,397,398],{},"false",[186,400,401,404],{},[200,402,403],{},"Experimental."," Stdio contract — see below",[154,406,408],{"id":407},"environment","Environment",[141,410,411],{},"Every container gets:",[413,414,415,422,428],"ul",{},[416,417,418,421],"li",{},[145,419,420],{},"SCHED_RUN_ID"," — the run id",[416,423,424,427],{},[145,425,426],{},"SCHED_TASK_NAME"," — the task name",[416,429,430,432,433,435,436,439,440,443,444,446,447,449,450,453,454,230,457,460],{},[145,431,294],{}," → each top-level key as ",[145,434,312],{}," env var (",[145,437,438],{},"{ \"userId\": 42 }"," →\n",[145,441,442],{},"USER_ID=42",") plus ",[145,445,316],{}," with the full JSON. Static ",[145,448,283],{}," wins over data-derived vars.\nTwo data keys that map to the same env var (",[145,451,452],{},"fooBar"," and ",[145,455,456],{},"foo_bar",[145,458,459],{},"FOO_BAR",") are an error:\nconfig validation fails fast at load time, and a run that slips through fails instead of\nsilently last-write-wins.",[154,462,464],{"id":463},"exit-codes","Exit codes",[159,466,467,477],{},[162,468,469],{},[165,470,471,474],{},[168,472,473],{},"Exit",[168,475,476],{},"Result",[181,478,479,491,506],{},[165,480,481,486],{},[186,482,483],{},[145,484,485],{},"0",[186,487,488],{},[145,489,490],{},"succeeded",[165,492,493,496],{},[186,494,495],{},"non-zero",[186,497,498,501,502,505],{},[145,499,500],{},"failed"," with ",[145,503,504],{},"exit N"," + tail of the log",[165,507,508,511],{},[186,509,510],{},"timeout",[186,512,513,514],{},"SIGTERM → SIGKILL → ",[145,515,336],{},[141,517,518,521,522,524,525,528,529,532],{},[145,519,520],{},"config.timeoutMs: -1"," disables the container timeout entirely — the process\nruns until it exits on its own or is cancelled manually. (Before daemon 0.11.0 a\n",[145,523,340],{}," was passed straight into ",[145,526,527],{},"setTimeout"," and killed the container instantly\nwith ",[145,530,531],{},"timeout after -1ms",".)",[154,534,536,537,540],{"id":535},"stdio-contract-envelope-true-experimental","Stdio contract (",[145,538,539],{},"envelope: true",") — experimental",[542,543,544],"blockquote",{},[141,545,546,548,549,553],{},[200,547,403],{}," The ",[382,550,552],{"href":551},"process","process runner"," ships a reference worker for the\nstdio contract; a container image that speaks it is not published yet. Enable it\nwhen your own image implements the contract (see below) — exit-code mode remains\nthe default and is unchanged.",[141,555,556,557,561],{},"Opt-in protocol mode for containers that want to report progress and results\nstructurally. The container speaks the ",[382,558,560],{"href":559},"..\u002Fprotocol#stdio-transport","stdio transport",":",[413,563,564,582,595,604],{},[416,565,566,569,570,573,574,577,578,581],{},[200,567,568],{},"request"," — one JSON envelope ",[145,571,572],{},"{ \"task\": { \"name\", \"config\" }, \"data\" }"," on\n",[200,575,576],{},"stdin"," (",[145,579,580],{},"docker run -i",", attached automatically), then EOF",[416,583,584,587,588,591,592],{},[200,585,586],{},"progress"," — NDJSON lines on ",[200,589,590],{},"stdout",": intermediate\n",[145,593,594],{},"{ \"status\": \"running\", \"progress\": 42 }",[416,596,597,600,601,603],{},[200,598,599],{},"result"," — one terminal line on ",[200,602,590],{}," (same envelope shape as the process\nrunner \u002F HTTP runner)",[416,605,606,609,610,613],{},[200,607,608],{},"logs"," — anything else on ",[200,611,612],{},"stderr"," (never stdout — stdout is the protocol)",[615,616,621],"pre",{"className":617,"code":618,"language":619,"meta":620,"style":620},"language-json shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter vitesse-light vitesse-dark","{ \"runner\": \"docker\", \"config\": { \"image\": \"registry\u002Fmy-worker\", \"envelope\": true, \"data\": { \"videoId\": \"v-42\" } } }\n","json","",[145,622,623],{"__ignoreMap":620},[243,624,627,631,635,639,642,644,647,650,652,655,657,659,661,663,666,668,671,673,675,677,680,682,684,686,688,690,692,696,698,700,702,704,706,708,710,714,716,718,720,723,725,728,730],{"class":625,"line":626},"line",1,[243,628,630],{"class":629},"soVBu","{",[243,632,634],{"class":633},"s4Jsk"," \"",[243,636,638],{"class":637},"sLorS","runner",[243,640,641],{"class":633},"\"",[243,643,561],{"class":629},[243,645,634],{"class":646},"sbYkP",[243,648,147],{"class":649},"sTbE_",[243,651,641],{"class":646},[243,653,654],{"class":629},",",[243,656,634],{"class":633},[243,658,156],{"class":637},[243,660,641],{"class":633},[243,662,561],{"class":629},[243,664,665],{"class":629}," {",[243,667,634],{"class":633},[243,669,190],{"class":670},"sa2tF",[243,672,641],{"class":633},[243,674,561],{"class":629},[243,676,634],{"class":646},[243,678,679],{"class":649},"registry\u002Fmy-worker",[243,681,641],{"class":646},[243,683,654],{"class":629},[243,685,634],{"class":633},[243,687,392],{"class":670},[243,689,641],{"class":633},[243,691,561],{"class":629},[243,693,695],{"class":694},"s8XtY"," true",[243,697,654],{"class":629},[243,699,634],{"class":633},[243,701,294],{"class":670},[243,703,641],{"class":633},[243,705,561],{"class":629},[243,707,665],{"class":629},[243,709,634],{"class":633},[243,711,713],{"class":712},"skNjk","videoId",[243,715,641],{"class":633},[243,717,561],{"class":629},[243,719,634],{"class":646},[243,721,722],{"class":649},"v-42",[243,724,641],{"class":646},[243,726,727],{"class":629}," }",[243,729,727],{"class":629},[243,731,732],{"class":629}," }\n",[141,734,735,736,738],{},"A container that opted in but exits without a terminal envelope is a broken worker: the\nrun fails with a clear protocol error. A container without ",[145,737,392],{}," keeps the plain\nexit-code mapping — the two modes never mix.",[154,740,742],{"id":741},"private-registries-auth","Private registries (auth)",[141,744,745,746,577,749,751,752,755,756,561],{},"The runner spawns the ",[200,747,748],{},"docker CLI",[145,750,151],{},"), not the docker HTTP API — so\nCLI credential resolution applies. ",[145,753,754],{},"docker run"," pulls an image that is not present\nlocally, and that implicit pull authenticates exactly like ",[145,757,758],{},"docker pull",[413,760,761,783,801,808],{},[416,762,763,766,767,770,771,774,775,778,779,782],{},[200,764,765],{},"The CLI must exist in the daemon's image."," The official ",[145,768,769],{},"sched-daemon"," image\nships ",[145,772,773],{},"docker-cli"," (added 2026-08-22 after books' T2 finding); a custom\u002Fcomposed\nimage that drops it needs ",[145,776,777],{},"apk add docker-cli"," (alpine) — otherwise every\ndocker task fails with ",[145,780,781],{},"ENOENT"," at spawn.",[416,784,785,788,789,792,793,796,797,800],{},[145,786,787],{},"$DOCKER_CONFIG\u002Fconfig.json"," (default ",[145,790,791],{},"~\u002F.docker\u002Fconfig.json",") — mount it into the\ndaemon's container (",[145,794,795],{},"\u002Froot\u002F.docker\u002Fconfig.json",") or point ",[145,798,799],{},"DOCKER_CONFIG"," at a volume.",[416,802,803,804,807],{},"The same file that ",[145,805,806],{},"docker login"," writes — no sched-side config, no env creds.",[416,809,810,811,814],{},"Works unchanged behind a read-only docker-socket proxy (",[145,812,813],{},"DOCKER_HOST","): credentials\nare a CLI-side concern, the proxy passes the pull through.",[141,816,817,818,577,821,824,825,828,829,831,832,834],{},"The image allowlist is matched ",[200,819,820],{},"by name\u002Fcommand string only",[145,822,823],{},"image[@command]",");\nregistry auth never affects allowlist matching or tag resolution (default ",[145,826,827],{},":latest",",\nexplicit ",[145,830,214],{}," wins — pure string logic). The actual tag dereference happens at pull\ntime inside the docker daemon, which is exactly where the credentials apply. A pull\nthat fails auth surfaces as a run failure (",[145,833,754],{}," exits non-zero with the\nregistry's 401 in the log).",[154,836,838,839,207],{"id":837},"security-sandbox-allowedtools","Security: sandbox (",[145,840,367],{},[141,842,843,844,846,847,850,851,853,854,857,858,861],{},"The runner is constrained by the sandbox ceiling — pass ",[145,845,367],{}," when\ncreating the runner (or set it in the daemon build \u002F tasks.json ",[145,848,849],{},"runners"," block,\nsee ",[382,852,385],{"href":384},"). Exact names and trailing wildcards are supported:\n",[145,855,856],{},"allowedTools: ['alpine:*', 'ghcr.io\u002Fmy-org\u002F*']",". A task whose image\u002Fcommand is\nnot allowed fails fast ",[200,859,860],{},"before"," any container is spawned.",[141,863,864,865,868,869,871,872,875],{},"A ceiling spec with a command dimension (",[145,866,867],{},"alpine@echo",") also blocks tasks that\nomit an explicit